# The build context is tarred up and sent to the builder before the first COPY runs,
# so without this the multi-gigabyte `target/` directory is transferred on every
# build. The Dockerfile copies only the manifests, `src/` and `benches/`; everything
# else here is either output or analysis state.
/target
/.scratch
/tmp
/tests/e2e/node_modules
/local
.smtc-cache/
.git
